 in `attention-combine` is loose: `carry.ts` only filters focus on a single gloss and does not call `combineAttention`. Only `merge.ts` combines, and that path covers squash and carry-of-a-range (**read**; the squash test passes, **verified**).\n\n**2. Misgraded necessity**\n- `focus-validation` [required] is overgraded. The task is declaring and displaying attention. Rejecting unknown or repeated focus ids is a well-formedness guard, which makes it defensive. It could fold into `schema-fields` or be labelled `defensive`. It is cheap and worth keeping (**verified**: the \"add refuses … unknown focus\" test passes).\n- `note-format-4` [required] is correctly graded. The rollout requirement is real (**read**, see above).\n- `html-display` and `show-display` [required] are fine; display is part of the stated task.\n\n**3. Removal candidates**\n- None needed. Dropping `focus-validation` would only let bad ids reach `show` and the HTML view. Carry and merge already drop ids for groups that are gone.\n\n**4. Simplifications**\n- None needed. `combineAttention` is small and readable.\n\n**5. Missing risks**\n- **(read)** `groupLink` in `src/html/client.js:36` builds an anchor for any id with no check against the groups present. A focus id that names no group would render as a dead link. Validation on `add` makes this unlikely, but carried or hand-edited notes are not re-validated.\n- **(read)** Rollout scope is per-note. A single format-4 commit in a range makes old `show <range>`, `html` and `ary` fail for that range, not only for that commit. The author's rollout note says \"reports … until upgraded\", which understates how much one note can block.\n- The unrated-contamination rule (rated plus unrated squash becomes unrated) is disclosed by the author, so I am not counting it as a new risk. It does make a useful rating look like no guidance, so it is worth a line in the release notes.\n- `override_reason` is kept only from parts at the combined level (verified by the test). This is a design choice, not a defect.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
