","f0fa17b771d8eec8","f29ea9c90baf6588","f2e2ce12a68da250","f34f7b6523a0a7a1","f544a9373a068640","f5d84364c3da9466","f629ecfe817d7da8","f66dc4b5e031c253","f7677ab50f9190a3","f7d8bcef995ed44d","f885a4eb6f72fd7b","fa1a49fb68c21eca","fa947b9394e6d2cf","fa991bc5506b1269","fac74522977b221e","fb177f54a0c88496","fb2707c000a64e72","fc6356802a63ea42","fc77422c4be8fa93","fde7932fcf93056c","ff1a4bf1ae64ae47","ff1a4bf1ae64ae47","ff66d4a449c00b40"],"groups":["4b46ba8e142021cf","5ac51bf06a3e0ac6","8e3d6a550157053d","2b2071572f551f27","8dfc5b9d3527a7cd","b8a31ff216a91db5","ff3f3f384b991065","5c2aab2cc6d30ef9","7c9050e74d184a1b","b5f44ad91e7a4e1c","40c5fe121ce7eff3","31537aeaf5b5ace0"],"findings":"**Review of the uncommitted attention/impact change**\n\nI ran `test/attention.test.ts` (11/11 pass). I did not get a clean run of `test/gloss.test.ts` or the full `npm test` here: both timed out in this environment. Findings below are marked **verified** (I ran something that shows it) or **read** (from the code only).\n\n**1. Mismatch: the attention badge inherits the banner's box style (verified)**\nThe HTML banner is `el('section', 'attention')`, but `levelBadge('attention', a.level)` gives the badge the class `badge attention`. The CSS rule `.attention { display:flex; padding; border; background; max-width }` therefore also applies to the badge. I generated the page from a scratch repo with `git gloss html` and screenshotted it with headless Chromium. The `CAREFUL` badge renders as a bordered box inside the banner, unlike the other pill badges. The fix is to rename the banner class (for example `attention-banner`) or the badge kind. Group `html-display`.\n\n**2. Mismatch: squashing a rated commit with an unrated one reports a lower level than the change warrants (verified)**\nGroup `attention-combine` says the level is the maximum of the sources. In `merge.ts`, `rated` filters out sources with no `attention`, so an unglossed part contributes nothing. I built a squash of a `skim` rename commit and an unglossed logic change. `git gloss carry` warned that h2 was \"not explained by the sources\", yet the written note still has `attention: { level: 'skim' }`, and `show` prints `attention: SKIM`. The author's risk note covers only the case where a source's groups are all dropped. It does not cover unrated sources, and the combined note is not marked as incomplete. Possible fixes: treat an unrated, non-empty source as `must-read`, or add a warning or reason to the note. Group `attention-combine`.\n\n**3. Misgrading: `show-display` bundles scope beyond \"display\" (read)**\n`--sort impact` and the impact form of `--only` are not display of the declared fields. They change the flag's semantics (`--only` now matches on two kinds, and naming both kinds means a group must match both). They add about 30 lines plus tests. Removing them would not affect the stated task. Group `show-display` is labelled `required`. I would label these parts `incidental` or split them into their own group. Expected impact of removal: no loss to the declared fields, and `--only` keeps its old behaviour.\n\n**4. Misgrading: `note-format-4` is a compatibility guard (read)**\nThe guard prevents old readers from silently dropping the new fields on carry. That is worth keeping, but it is a rollout safeguard rather than something the task needs. Label it `defensive`, or keep `required` with that reason. I read the old check at `HEAD~1:src/schema.ts:234` (`data.gloss > NOTE_FORMAT`), which does refuse format 4. I did not re-run the \"checked by hand\" claim.\n\n**5. Misgrading (minor): `attention-combine` as `required` (read)**\nThe task statement names carry and merge, so `required` is defensible. The merge/carry code is larger than the schema change it depends on, and the `rename` callback and `override_reason` union are the parts most open to simplification.\n\n**6. Simplification (read)**\n`combineAttention` takes a `rename(part, id)` callback plus the `groups` array only to look up impact. Passing an impact lookup or the already-renamed focus lists would make the function simpler to follow. This is optional.\n\n**7. Missing risks (read)**\n- Finding 2 above is the main one.\n- Format-4 notes fail on older readers in a way that can break `ary`, `html` and the hooks. The author lists this, so it is accurate.\n\n**Accurate annotations (read)**\n- `schema-fields`, `focus-validation`, `docs`, and the `carry` focus filtering match the code.\n- `git gloss schema` does list `impact` and `impact_reason`.\n- The `--only` / `--sort` rejection paths behave as the tests state.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
