7","ff66d4a449c00b40"],"groups":["4b46ba8e142021cf","5ac51bf06a3e0ac6","8e3d6a550157053d","2b2071572f551f27","8dfc5b9d3527a7cd","b8a31ff216a91db5","ff3f3f384b991065","5c2aab2cc6d30ef9","7c9050e74d184a1b","b5f44ad91e7a4e1c"],"findings":"Five suggestions, ranked by benefit for the effort. All are **read** only; I changed nothing in the clone and ran nothing.\n\n1. **Remove `higherImpact`, `src/attention.ts:6` (group `attention-combine`).** It is exported but nothing uses it (checked with `grep`: the only hit is its own definition). That is dead code, about 2 lines.\n\n2. **Drop the `order` bookkeeping in `combineAttention`, `src/attention.ts:20-24`.** `Array.prototype.sort` is stable, so the `.map((id, order) => …)` and the `|| a.order - b.order` tie-break do nothing. This is enough:\n   ```ts\n   const focus = [...new Set(...)].sort((a, b) => impactRank(impactOf.get(b)) - impactRank(impactOf.get(a))).slice(0, 3)\n   ```\n   It is about 4 lines shorter and has one less concept. The ties-in-order case in the `combineAttention` test would still check it.\n\n3. **Parse `--only` once, `src/commands/show.ts` (group `show-display`).**\n   - **Problem:** `(NECESSITY as readonly string[]).includes` and the matching `IMPACT` cast appear in three places. They are the unknown-value check in `run` and the two partitions in `matchesOnly`. `matchesOnly` also re-partitions `only` for every commit and group.\n   - **Fix:** build `{ necessities, impacts }` once in `run`. Do the unknown check on the leftovers, and pass that object to `renderCommit` instead of `string[]`. `matchesOnly` then becomes the one-line predicate it already returns.\n   - **Size:** about 10 lines, and it removes the repeated casts.\n\n4. **Pull the impact cell out of the row template, `src/commands/show.ts:222` (group `show-display`).**\n   - **Problem:** the row string now holds a nested ternary, `' '.repeat(11 - impact.length - 2)` and a second `' '.repeat(11)`. The `11` is the width of `[sensitive]` and is also hardcoded into `intentCol`.\n   - **Fix:** a small `impactCell(g, impactW)` helper, or `impactTag(i) + ' '.repeat(IMPACT_W - i.length - 2)` with a named `IMPACT_W = 11`. `necessityWord(n, pad)` already takes a pad argument, so `impactTag(i, pad)` would match that pattern.\n   - **Why:** the next reader can see that the width ties to the longest impact name. It is a clarity change of about 5 lines.\n\n5. **Build the focus list directly in `carryGloss`, `src/carry.ts:71-72` (group `attention-combine`).** It currently spreads, filters, then `delete`s a key from the object it just built. Compute `const focus = a.attention?.focus?.filter((id) => keptIds.has(id))`, then:\n   ```ts\n   const attention = a.attention && { ...a.attention, focus: undefined, ...(focus?.length ? { focus } : {}) }\n   ```\n   or use a destructuring rest. Either avoids mutating after construction. It is a small clarity change.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
