","f0fa17b771d8eec8","f29ea9c90baf6588","f2e2ce12a68da250","f34f7b6523a0a7a1","f544a9373a068640","f5d84364c3da9466","f629ecfe817d7da8","f66dc4b5e031c253","f7677ab50f9190a3","f7d8bcef995ed44d","f885a4eb6f72fd7b","fa1a49fb68c21eca","fa947b9394e6d2cf","fa991bc5506b1269","fac74522977b221e","fb177f54a0c88496","fb2707c000a64e72","fc6356802a63ea42","fc77422c4be8fa93","fde7932fcf93056c","ff1a4bf1ae64ae47","ff1a4bf1ae64ae47","ff66d4a449c00b40"],"groups":["4b46ba8e142021cf","5ac51bf06a3e0ac6","8e3d6a550157053d","2b2071572f551f27","8dfc5b9d3527a7cd","b8a31ff216a91db5","ff3f3f384b991065","5c2aab2cc6d30ef9","7c9050e74d184a1b","b5f44ad91e7a4e1c","40c5fe121ce7eff3","31537aeaf5b5ace0","e5e91357c7cffc7e"],"findings":"## Review of uncommitted attention & impact work (snapshot 7fc947e)\n\nI ran `test/attention.test.ts` directly: 11 of 11 pass. The full `npm test` run did not finish within my window, so `test/gloss.test.ts` (the 4→5 edit) is unverified by running. Everything else below comes from reading the code, except where marked.\n\n### 1. Mismatches\nNone found. The annotations match the code for schema, validation, format 4, carry, merge, show, html and docs. Two wording points:\n- `docs` / SKILL.md says `impact_reason` is \"at `contract` and above\". The schema only says \"expected for contract and sensitive\" and does not enforce it. Consistent in spirit, but not a rule the tool checks. **read**\n- The README says \"A gloss that doesn't use them is still written in its old format.\" **verified** by the `a note is format 4 only when it uses the new fields` test.\n\n### 2. Misgraded necessity\n- `note-format-4` [required]: I accept this. Bumping `NOTE_FORMAT` to 4 is the only way old readers refuse rather than drop the fields. The author's refusal claim holds: at `b3aac37` `NOTE_FORMAT = 3` and `readNote` throws \"written by a newer git-gloss\" for any higher format. **read**\n- `attention-combine` [required]: accurate. Carry and merge would otherwise lose or misdirect `attention`.\n- `docs` [supporting] and `tests` [supporting] are correctly graded.\n\n### 3. Removal candidates\nNone worth removing. The `show` impact column and `--sort`/`--only` extensions are the largest surface. They are labelled required, but they are not strictly needed for the stated task: \"declared fields would be stored but invisible in the terminal\" holds only for the `show` attention header. Deferring the `--sort`/`--only impact` part would cut roughly 30 lines of `show.ts`. It is a judgment call, not a defect.\n\n### 4. Simplifications\n- `combineAttention` calls `ATTENTION.indexOf` twice in the max reduction. An `attentionRank` helper, parallel to `impactRank`, would read more consistently. Minor.\n- `carry.ts:73` writes `focus: undefined` into the object rather than omitting the key. Harmless (JSON drops it), but `({ focus: undefined })`-style cleanup would match the rest of the file's spread-conditional idiom. Minor.\n\n### 5. Missing risks\n- **Silent under-rating after a mixed squash (the author's last listed risk, but it should not ship as \"intended\").** **read**: `merge.ts:183` builds `rated` from sources that have `attention`, and `combineAttention` takes the max over those alone. A squash of a `skim` commit plus an unrated commit that contains real logic therefore displays `attention: SKIM`. That is a wrong answer shown to the reviewer, not a gap. Phase 2's floor does not fix this for phase 1. Suggested fix: if any used source is unrated, omit `attention` (so it shows \"unrated\") or floor the level to `look`. The author should choose, but the current behaviour is worse than either.\n- **Rollout (author listed it; the mechanism is confirmed).** **read**: the `readNote` refusal applies to `show`, `carry`, `html`, `ary` and merge paths via `loader.ts:70`. Sync does not validate notes (`sync.ts:22`), so a format-4 note is pushed to remotes and reaches older clients, which then refuse it on `show`. Users of older clients will see errors on commits that are fine, not just on the new fields. Worth a changelog line.\n- **Focus rename on squash ignores focus ids of unrated sources.** Not a bug, since unrated sources contribute no focus. It is the same root cause as the first risk above.\n\nTest status: attention tests 11/11 **verified**. `gloss.test.ts` and the full suite not run to completion.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
