","fa1a49fb68c21eca","fa947b9394e6d2cf","fa991bc5506b1269","fac74522977b221e","fb177f54a0c88496","fb2707c000a64e72","fc6356802a63ea42","fc77422c4be8fa93","fde7932fcf93056c","ff1a4bf1ae64ae47","ff1a4bf1ae64ae47","ff66d4a449c00b40"],"groups":["4b46ba8e142021cf","5ac51bf06a3e0ac6","8e3d6a550157053d","2b2071572f551f27","8dfc5b9d3527a7cd","b8a31ff216a91db5","ff3f3f384b991065","5c2aab2cc6d30ef9","7c9050e74d184a1b","b5f44ad91e7a4e1c"],"findings":"## Review of the attention/impact Phase 1 commit (8010da2)\n\nRan the suite (`npm test`: 133 pass, 0 fail) and `tsc --noEmit` (clean). The working tree is clean and the changes are in HEAD, so I reviewed `HEAD~1..HEAD`.\n\n**Mismatches**\n\nNone found. The annotations match the code on every point I checked.\n\n- **note-format-4 \"checked by hand against the pre-change CLI\"**: **verified**. I built the pre-change CLI from `HEAD~1` in a scratch worktree and ran `show` on a note written by the new CLI with `impact` and `attention`. It printed `written by a newer git-gloss (format 4); upgrade to read it`. The worktree is removed.\n- **show-display \"attention: unrated\" and the impact column only when some group declares one**: **verified** by the tests and by reading `render`/`show.ts`.\n- **html-display**: **verified** in headless Chromium. I generated a rated gloss, screenshotted the page, and the banner, the \"look here first: risky\" link, the MUST-READ badge, the impact badges and the `impact:` fact all render in the dark theme. No console errors appeared in the Chromium log. Only the dark theme and one commit were checked, not light mode or a branch page with several commits.\n- **focus-validation and carry focus filtering**: **read**. `validate.ts` checks `groupIds`, and `carry.ts` filters focus by `keptIds`. Both are covered by tests.\n- **attention-combine merge mapping**: **read**. `merge.ts` maps `rated[part]` (a source index) through `newId`, which is keyed by the same source index, so the mapping is consistent.\n\n**Misgraded necessity**\n\n1. **attention-combine (required, serves: task): the group is mostly right, but h4 is shared.** `src/attention.ts` also exports `impactRank`, which `src/commands/show.ts` imports for `--sort impact`. So h4 serves show-display as well as the merge path. **read** (grep for the import). Suggested fix: keep h4 under attention-combine but list `show-display` in its `serves`, or move `impactRank` into a file the show group owns. This is a bookkeeping issue, not a behaviour one.\n\n**Removal candidates**\n\n2. **`override_reason` (schema-fields)**: nothing enforces or derives it. Phase 1 has no under-rating checks, so it only carries author text through to display. Dropping it would cost little, but it is part of the requested attention object, so keep it unless you want the schema smaller. Impact: low.\n\n**Simplifications**\n\nNone needed. `combineAttention` is short and clear.\n\n**Missing risks**\n\n3. **`--only` mixes kinds with AND semantics, which the usage text does not say.** `--only mechanical,sensitive` returns nothing, while `--only contract,sensitive` ORs within the impact kind. The usage line `--only <necessity|impact,...>` and the README sentence \"impact values work too\" don't state that a group must match each kind named. **verified** by the test (`--only mechanical,sensitive` → exit 1). Add one clause to the usage or README.\n4. **HTML multi-commit and branch views are untested in a browser.** The banner is added to each commit body, and the tests only cover a single commit. **read**.\n5. **Attention is self-declared with no floor.** The author lists this. Nothing stops a `sensitive` change from being rated `skim`. This is accepted for Phase 1 but should be tracked as the next item.\n6. **Impact column width uses all groups, not the shown ones.** `impactW` is computed from `gloss.groups`, so `--only` can show a blank column. Cosmetic. **read**.\n\nI did not verify the claim that `fixup` drops attention without the change. I did not find a fixup path in `src`, so that part of the attention-combine \"if removed\" text is **read** only.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
